# debian/control.in -- templated at build time from packaging/lib/identity.mjs.
#
# `Depends` lists Electron's *system* shared libraries only. The two rules that
# matter, both asserted by tests/integration/packaging/deb-contract.test.mjs:
#   - no `nodejs` / `golang` / `python3` (a clean machine must never need a
#     toolchain: everything is bundled under /opt/ordessa, FR-071);
#   - every listed library is one the shipped Electron binary actually links
#     against, so the package does not demand more than it uses.
#
# The `t64` variants are the Ubuntu 24.04+ time_t transition names; the plain
# names are kept as alternates so the package installs on 22.04/24.04 both.

Package: @PKG@
Version: @VERSION@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: @AUTHOR@
Homepage: @HOMEPAGE@
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends:
 libc6,
 libgtk-3-0 | libgtk-3-0t64,
 libnotify4,
 libnss3,
 libnspr4,
 libasound2 | libasound2t64,
 libgbm1,
 libxkbcommon0,
 libxkbfile1,
 libdrm2,
 libatspi2.0-0 | libatspi2.0-0t64,
 libatk1.0-0 | libatk1.0-0t64,
 libatk-bridge2.0-0 | libatk-bridge2.0-0t64,
 libcups2 | libcups2t64,
 libdbus-1-3,
 libexpat1,
 libx11-6,
 libxcb1,
 libxcomposite1,
 libxdamage1,
 libxext6,
 libxfixes3,
 libxrandr2,
 libpango-1.0-0,
 libcairo2,
 xdg-utils,
 policykit-1 | polkitd | polkitd-pkla
Recommends:
 fonts-liberation
Suggests:
Description: @DESCRIPTION@
 Ordessa is the Ordessa desktop product: an Electron shell, the bundled
 Server runtime and the ACP bridge, installed as one self-contained package.
 .
 Everything needed to run is shipped under /opt/ordessa (fixed-version
 CPython, the verified Server dependency closure, the ACP bridge and the
 prebuilt Electron application), so installation requires no compiler, no
 language toolchain and no manual configuration.
 .
 Updates are signed (Ed25519) and delivered from a static update channel;
 the application verifies the signed manifest, the package hash and the data
 compatibility floor before it installs anything.
